  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Access to Menstrual Products in East Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Menstrual stigma, lack of access to menstrual products, and low education on reproductive health are putting girls&apos; and women&apos;s health at risk. It also limits their life opportunities and, therefore, opportunities for their families and communities. This is worse in low socio-economic and rural communities in Tanzania and Kenya. Over 70% of women said they couldn&apos;t afford menstrual products for their last period. Femme International is working to support these communities.</narrative>
  </description>
